Berlin for mr. Toomey Berlin is like  Barcelona it's a multicultural city this  room for everybody the mood on the  streets it feels like home - the weather  but otherwise it's much the same again  eggwin Arriba is the head chef Giovanna  Gonzalez miranda is the host together  they are the creative minds behind the  gastro bar - qua the concept is imported  from Spain small servings made for  sharing any relaxed ambience no she she  just finds Spanish cuisine the gastro  bar and the idea behind it it was like  to do something pretty informal  something like gastronomic like really  haikus in the world where I was working  before but to make it accessible for bit  for people it's kind of democratizing  the Haiku scene so try to do something  like a restaurant but with the  atmosphere of the bar  agar or iguana Riva was born in Spain's  Basque region in 1972 he worked as a  dishwasher to finance his English  studies in Ireland there he acquired a  taste for gastronomy and trained as a  chef he came to Berlin in 2005 here he  gathered experience in a number of fine  restaurants then tip qua gave him free  rein to go wild in the kitchen he bases  his creative experiments on Spanish  Basque culinary tradition I was born in  in a place that is called the arnica and  quite close to the sea when I was child  we were going to the harbor and you were  I was just really amazed by all the  fishermen bring you know the food and  the smell of the fish and then in the  restaurants in the harbor they were used  to cook this this traditional recipe  bacalao our pupil is a traditional dish  from the Basque region bacalao is  Spanish for salted cod the dish calls  for dried and salted fish soaked in  water for two days before it's cooked  that makes it easier to process and  gives it its special taste  you don't need a lot of ingredients for  bacalao a pill pill but you do need  sensitivity and good timing what special  is making mayonnaise from the gelatin of  the fish skin it's produced by slow  cooking making sure that oil doesn't get  too hot the emulsion arising from the  oil and gelatin is called real pill the  dish is a popular delicacy in tip quark  and the recipe has a colorful origin the  fishermen used to go to to cut this cord  to call water and the north and they  used to cut it and part of them they  were put in advance on salt for the  conservation of the of the fish and part  of them they used to put it in the oil  and the movement of the of the boat  actually created this incredible sauce  which is actually just oil and the  gelatin of the fish  Giovanni Gonzales Miranda was born in  Chile in 1983 when he was a youth his  family moved to Barcelona in 2011 he  came to Berlin two years later he and a  river opened the tip qualm  the name is Basque and means Cosa corner  it also refers to when friends come  together to cook and party  [Music]  along with the regular menu tip cooler  has daily specials Giovanni Gonzalez  Miranda acts as sommelier helping guests  choose the right wines  Tipler stocks wines from all over the  world for me wine is more than a drink  it's culture it's the landscape the  earth it's part of a region you don't  know but when you close your eyes you  think yes I know what direction this  comes from it's part of the earth the  two friends found a suitable place for  their gastro bar on a corner in Berlin  smokerin district at first tip car was  only open in the evenings but now it  also offers a lunch menu or cozinha para  vosotros baccala bill bill espero que  vota controversial
 

